 [evidence record](../docs/phase-2/experiment-results/canonical-final-smoke.json)
 preserves the result outside the ignored sweep output.
 
+Refresh the five decision-facing headline comparisons with a fresh flat-fee
+control for every load:
+
+```console
+./scripts/run_canonical_headlines.sh
+```
+
+This runs the canonical and flat-fee variants over seeds 0–9 for 2,000 slots
+at low, mid, severe-congestion, EB-capacity-stress, and launch-day load (100
+summary-only simulations). It writes five sweep summaries with their effective
+configs and selected loads, plus
+`sweep-results/canonical-headlines/comparison.md` and `comparison.json`. The
+comparison records the Git revision and whether the simulator worktree was
+clean; for a dirty run it also preserves an applyable `source.patch` and its
+SHA-256. It records the built simulator's SHA-256 before starting the sweeps,
+so the executed artifact remains identifiable even if the worktree changes
+during a long run. The runner refuses to overwrite an existing result
+directory; use `--out DIR` for a subsequent refresh.
+
+This manifest opts into separate deterministic RNG streams for fresh-demand
+sampling, ranking-block production, and retry jitter. A paired seed therefore
+keeps the exogenous demand samples and block opportunities fixed even when the
+two mechanisms produce different retry flows. Other manifests default to the
+legacy shared stream, preserving the seeded sequence used by archived-reference
+smoke checks.
+
+This is a fresh estimate for the current canonical D16/K10 model, not a promise
+to reproduce the historical numbers exactly: four of the five published rows
+used the older D8 anchor, and splitting the RNG streams changes the seeded
+sequences. The generated report states these scope differences explicitly.
+
